<title>JAPAN: S'tomo Metal says to cut Q1 stainless steel output.</title>
<headline>S'tomo Metal says to cut Q1 stainless steel output.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sumitomo Metal Industries Ltd said on Wednesday that it would cut its stainless steel output in the April-June period by 10 percent against the previous quarter.</p>
<p>Sumitomo did not disclose how many tonnes of stainless steel it would produce during the period and said this was a matter of policy.</p>
<p>A company official said the firm had decided to cut output to push up domestic stainless prices. -- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7391</p>
